WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:01.767
-Thank you for being here, bud.

00:00:01.767 --> 00:00:03.968
Man, people love you.

00:00:03.968 --> 00:00:05.033
-Good evening!

00:00:05.033 --> 00:00:08.067
Hello, New York.
-That feels good, right?

00:00:08.067 --> 00:00:11.400
That's got to feel good.
They love you.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:14.167
We ran into each other a few
months ago at a restaurant.

00:00:14.167 --> 00:00:15.467
-Oh, yeah.
-In L.A.

00:00:15.467 --> 00:00:16.901
Do you remember that?
-Of course I remember that.

00:00:16.901 --> 00:00:18.334
-Yeah, yeah. I didn't know.

00:00:18.334 --> 00:00:20.467
I saw you.
I saw you eating.

00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:22.534
You were with your girlfriend,
and I thought it would be funny.

00:00:22.534 --> 00:00:24.167
I sent you over --
-An olive.

00:00:24.167 --> 00:00:26.834
-One olive.
-One olive.

00:00:26.834 --> 00:00:30.067
-I go, split it, eat it
yourself, whatever you want.

00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:31.634
I don't want to tell you how to
eat your olive.

00:00:31.634 --> 00:00:33.734
-Yeah, and then what did we do?
We sent you something.

00:00:33.734 --> 00:00:35.133
-No, I'll tell you exactly
what you did.

00:00:35.133 --> 00:00:36.934
You had the whole restaurant

00:00:36.934 --> 00:00:38.667
come over and sing me
happy birthday.

00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:40.167
-Oh, yes.

00:00:40.167 --> 00:00:43.234
-And it was not my birthday.
It was not my birthday at all.

00:00:43.234 --> 00:00:45.234
[ Cheers and applause ]
I blew out the candle.

00:00:45.234 --> 00:00:48.300
I blew out the candle.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:51.667
It was not my birthday at all.
-It was not your birthday.

00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:54.934
-It was not my birthday, but
that really made me laugh.

00:00:54.934 --> 00:00:59.734
But then here's the best move.
You were leaving.

00:00:59.734 --> 00:01:04.968
There was a great guy who plays
music, guitar at the --

00:01:04.968 --> 00:01:07.667
-At the restaurant.
-At the restaurant.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:10.067
-We won't say where it is.
We don't want to give it away.

00:01:10.067 --> 00:01:13.801
And so he starts singing
"Hey Jude,"

00:01:13.801 --> 00:01:16.067
and so I jumped up
to sing with him.

00:01:16.067 --> 00:01:19.701
-You did.
-And I thought you were gone.

00:01:19.701 --> 00:01:21.367
-Well, no, we were still eating,

00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:23.367
and you were still singing
"Hey Jude."

00:01:23.367 --> 00:01:25.968
[ Laughter ]
And then they do that whole

00:01:25.968 --> 00:01:30.367
end part, you know, where it's
just "Nah, nah, nah, nah, nah."

00:01:30.367 --> 00:01:33.367
And you just kept going.
It was amazing.

00:01:33.367 --> 00:01:34.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:36.000
I mean, really.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:38.334
It was high, low.
-I was harmonizing with myself.

00:01:38.334 --> 00:01:40.434
-You were harmonizing.

00:01:40.434 --> 00:01:42.467
-But then you --
Were you just leaving?

00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:45.100
-Yeah, we were just leaving,
and then, you know --

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:47.701
-I grabbed you.
-Your energy, the whole

00:01:47.701 --> 00:01:50.367
audience, the audience --
the restaurant was into it.

00:01:50.367 --> 00:01:53.701
So, it was just like, let's all
sing, and we all started --

00:01:53.701 --> 00:01:55.934
-So we sang "Hey Jude" together.

00:01:55.934 --> 00:01:57.334
Yeah, it was fantastic.

00:01:57.334 --> 00:01:59.834
You have a great reputation
by the way, in Hollywood

00:01:59.834 --> 00:02:02.100
of being a very nice guy,
and I will say,

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:05.367
you always have been nice.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:05.367 --> 00:02:07.100
Always have been a cool guy
with me.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:10.067
-Fix my shirt. Fix my tie.

00:02:10.067 --> 00:02:11.901
-Yeah.
You've always been great to me.

00:02:11.901 --> 00:02:15.467
But I saw this photo
that just -- everyone is talking

00:02:15.467 --> 00:02:16.634
about it on the Internet.

00:02:16.634 --> 00:02:18.133
You crashed someone's wedding
in London.

00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:19.801
-I didn't crash --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.801 --> 00:02:21.767
-Well, it looks like
you weren't invited.

00:02:21.767 --> 00:02:24.167
I don't know.
-I sort of look like that.

00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:26.300
-I don't know if you crashed it,
but you definitely --

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:29.868
-I was invited to meet
some folks and take a photo.

00:02:29.868 --> 00:02:31.868
-Oh, sorry. So you heard people

00:02:31.868 --> 00:02:33.334
were getting married
or something?

00:02:33.334 --> 00:02:36.367
-No. It was outside and there
was another part of the hotel

00:02:36.367 --> 00:02:39.200
and it was outside of London
and they were having a wedding

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:42.267
and then the groom came by and
he was like, "Hi,"

00:02:42.267 --> 00:02:44.334
and I was like, "Hi."
And then he was like,

00:02:44.334 --> 00:02:46.067
"Do you want to take a picture
with everybody?"

00:02:46.067 --> 00:02:47.467
And I said,
"Yeah, sure, let's do it."

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:49.734
And meet some folks and we went
in there and I said

00:02:49.734 --> 00:02:53.234
hi and hi and hi and then we
took some photographs.

00:02:53.234 --> 00:02:55.133
That's one of the photographs.
-It made their night.

00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:58.434
-One of these things
does not belong and it was me.

00:02:58.434 --> 00:03:01.801
-I would have sang "Hey Jude"
with them if they asked me.

00:03:01.801 --> 00:03:03.400
-It was really lovely.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:04.968
-It's cool that you do
that stuff.

00:03:04.968 --> 00:03:06.834
It's also cool that you do
this stuff too.

00:03:06.834 --> 00:03:09.601
Can we talk about "Brzrkr"?
-Oh, you have "Brzrkr."

00:03:09.601 --> 00:03:12.667
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah, I have "Brzrkr."

00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:15.133
-It's a comic book.
-This is unbelievable.

00:03:15.133 --> 00:03:17.667
Now, this is just an idea you
had and you go,

00:03:17.667 --> 00:03:20.000
"I'm just going to make this."

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:21.934
-Yeah, I cowrote it with
Matt Kindt

00:03:21.934 --> 00:03:24.868
and amazing illustrator
Ron Garney.

00:03:24.868 --> 00:03:27.501
Issue 12. It's a 12-issue
limited series.

00:03:27.501 --> 00:03:29.567
The last one came out yesterday.

00:03:29.567 --> 00:03:31.200
-Yeah. Do you know the first --

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:32.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:32.968 --> 00:03:37.968
The first issue sold over
615,000 copies, making it

00:03:37.968 --> 00:03:41.300
the highest selling indie comic
of the 21st century.

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:43.367
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Wow. Thanks.

00:03:43.367 --> 00:03:45.133
Thanks, universe.
-Wow!

00:03:45.133 --> 00:03:47.400
-Thanks, everybody.
No, it's cool.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:49.834
I love comic books, and having
the chance to do something

00:03:49.834 --> 00:03:51.534
like that was really special.

00:03:51.534 --> 00:03:55.400
-How did you end up coming up
with a storyline and everything?

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:57.133
-Where do ideas come from?

00:03:57.133 --> 00:03:59.601
-I know, yeah,
that's a very deep question.

00:03:59.601 --> 00:04:02.801
-Where do they --
it came to me -- What about

00:04:02.801 --> 00:04:06.133
a character that could punch
people through the chest?

00:04:06.133 --> 00:04:09.801
And then, like, what if they
were half God, half immortal?

00:04:09.801 --> 00:04:13.701
And then what if they were alive
for 80,000 years?

00:04:13.701 --> 00:04:14.801
-What would you do
with this idea --

00:04:14.801 --> 00:04:16.634
-Then what would society do
with that

00:04:16.634 --> 00:04:19.367
but then he's cursed with
violence.

00:04:19.367 --> 00:04:21.501
-He doesn't want to be violent.
-He doesn't want to be violent.

00:04:21.501 --> 00:04:23.567
-No, but it's in his blood.
-He can't die.

00:04:23.567 --> 00:04:26.133
Then he doesn't know
who his father is.

00:04:26.133 --> 00:04:28.400
-Are you kidding me?
-There's this tribe that

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:31.734
asks the gods for a weapon
because they're being ambushed

00:04:31.734 --> 00:04:33.534
and exploited every season.

00:04:33.534 --> 00:04:36.033
And then they get this kid --
-When are we seeing this movie?

00:04:36.033 --> 00:04:37.634
I want to see this! Come on!

00:04:37.634 --> 00:04:40.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:40.734 --> 00:04:42.434
-Oh, and then he's, like,
being used by

00:04:42.434 --> 00:04:43.801
the United States government.

00:04:43.801 --> 00:04:45.434
They're trying to figure him
out.

00:04:45.434 --> 00:04:47.667
-Of course the government gets
involved. Yes.

00:04:47.667 --> 00:04:49.868
-Yes. Black ops.
-But what would you do with

00:04:49.868 --> 00:04:52.667
this idea, Keanu Reeves, if you
couldn't have this outlet?

00:04:52.667 --> 00:04:55.400
Would this just live
in your brain?

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:58.100
[ Laughter ]

00:04:58.100 --> 00:04:59.834
I don't know. You did it.
-I don't know.

00:04:59.834 --> 00:05:01.367
-You got it out.
-I don't know.

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:04.033
I mean, it's like
a creative act.

00:05:04.033 --> 00:05:06.667
It's something special.
-It is, yeah.

00:05:06.667 --> 00:05:08.234
-It's storytelling.

00:05:08.234 --> 00:05:11.601
And what would I do
if I couldn't do that?

00:05:11.601 --> 00:05:14.267
I'd probably be on
the street, just babbling.

00:05:14.267 --> 00:05:16.601
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:16.601 --> 00:05:19.367
Would you make this
into a movie?

00:05:19.367 --> 00:05:20.701
-Yeah, that would be fun.

00:05:20.701 --> 00:05:22.934
-Yeah. Would you direct it?

00:05:22.934 --> 00:05:25.701
-Mm. I don't know. I don't know.

00:05:25.701 --> 00:05:29.033
We tried to shop it around,
and then Netflix said,

00:05:29.033 --> 00:05:30.234
"Hey, do you want to make it
with us?"

00:05:30.234 --> 00:05:31.734
And I was like, "Sure."

00:05:31.734 --> 00:05:33.834
And then so we're going to try
and make that happen.

00:05:33.834 --> 00:05:35.601
-Whoa!

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:38.100
I love it.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:41.100
We have to talk about
"John Wick: Chapter 4."

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:42.834
Buddy, you did it again.

00:05:42.834 --> 00:05:44.267
It's unbelievable!

00:05:44.267 --> 00:05:47.601
It's -- This one --
This one's the best.

00:05:47.601 --> 00:05:49.367
-What?
-This one is the best one.

00:05:49.367 --> 00:05:50.834
Yes.
-The best? What?

00:05:50.834 --> 00:05:52.601
-Plug your ears because I know
they're all your babies.

00:05:52.601 --> 00:05:54.334
But I like this one.
-What? That's awesome.

00:05:54.334 --> 00:05:55.834
-The first one was like,
"Holy moly."

00:05:55.834 --> 00:05:57.200
-I know, what the heck is that?

00:05:57.200 --> 00:05:59.634
-I loved it. I didn't know
the first one was even out.

00:05:59.634 --> 00:06:01.367
I don't know how I even saw
the first one.

00:06:01.367 --> 00:06:03.801
And I go, "Oh, my gosh." I think
I was in a hotel somewhere.

00:06:03.801 --> 00:06:05.534
I go, "This movie is
phenomenal."

00:06:05.534 --> 00:06:07.567
I call my wife, I go, "You've
got to watch 'John Wick.'"

00:06:07.567 --> 00:06:10.133
I'm in all the way man,
and we love you,

00:06:10.133 --> 00:06:13.701
and the whole Fallons love
the Keanu at the house.

00:06:13.701 --> 00:06:16.000
Well, you celebrate my birthday
when it's not my birthday.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:17.334
It's great.

00:06:17.334 --> 00:06:20.234
This one has got it all.
It looks gorgeous.

00:06:20.234 --> 00:06:22.534
It's a work of art.

00:06:22.534 --> 00:06:25.567
The action starts maybe
five seconds into it

00:06:25.567 --> 00:06:28.300
and doesn't stop until you leave
the theater.

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:29.601
-Yeah, there's a lot of action.

00:06:29.601 --> 00:06:31.701
-You're on a horse at one point.

00:06:31.701 --> 00:06:33.033
-Yeah.
-Shooting people.

00:06:33.033 --> 00:06:35.200
-Well, you know, I'm -- Yeah.

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:36.200
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:37.834
There's nunchucks.

00:06:37.834 --> 00:06:39.033
-Yes, there are.
-Yeah.

00:06:39.033 --> 00:06:40.667
There's throwing stars.

00:06:40.667 --> 00:06:42.100
-Yeah.
-There's --

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:43.534
-Driving. Crazy driving.

00:06:43.534 --> 00:06:46.033
-By the way, driving scenes
with no doors.

00:06:46.033 --> 00:06:47.868
-Yeah, yeah.
-No windows maybe at one point.

00:06:47.868 --> 00:06:50.300
-They got blown out too.

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:53.634
-There's just a steering wheel
and wheels, that's all it is.

00:06:53.634 --> 00:06:54.801
It's like a go-cart at the end
of it.

00:06:54.801 --> 00:06:57.067
-It's an American muscle car.

00:06:57.067 --> 00:07:00.167
And throwing 180s.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:07:00.167 --> 00:07:01.634
-Doing John Wick things.

00:07:01.634 --> 00:07:04.601
-I read somewhere there's
14 action sequences.

00:07:04.601 --> 00:07:05.734
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:07:05.734 --> 00:07:08.234
-And it's all choreographed
brilliantly.

00:07:08.234 --> 00:07:09.868
-Yeah, most of the time.

00:07:09.868 --> 00:07:11.067
[ Laughter ]

00:07:11.067 --> 00:07:12.968
I mean, it's always --
Well, I can't say always.

00:07:12.968 --> 00:07:14.701
-Is there improvising ever?

00:07:14.701 --> 00:07:18.701
-Yeah, kind of, yeah.
-And does that end well?

00:07:18.701 --> 00:07:20.100
No?
-Yes.

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:23.033
No humans were harmed in
the making of this film.

00:07:23.033 --> 00:07:25.968
-Thank you, yeah.
-No, I mean, there's a lot --

00:07:25.968 --> 00:07:31.033
the director, visionary Chad
Stahelski, is very inventive.

00:07:31.033 --> 00:07:35.400
He really wants to create
different kinds of environments

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:39.434
or ways in the storytelling
for the action.

00:07:39.434 --> 00:07:41.300
-He's got to be a genius.

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:42.567
I mean, this is the fourth one.

00:07:42.567 --> 00:07:44.100
You're still inventing new ways
to go,

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:45.567
"Oh, that shot is gorgeous.

00:07:45.567 --> 00:07:47.033
How did he even come up
with that?"

00:07:47.033 --> 00:07:50.300
The cars on the side, the lights
hitting you at a certain thing.

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:51.934
-Cinema.

00:07:51.934 --> 00:07:54.434
-It feels like cinema.
-Cinema.

00:07:54.434 --> 00:07:56.901
-It feels like you're
watching -- Yes!

00:07:56.901 --> 00:07:59.868
-Cinema.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:59.868 --> 00:08:02.133
-What can we say about
"John Wick" and this one

00:08:02.133 --> 00:08:03.400
that's not spoiling anything?

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:08.200
Or can I just -- I know you want
to get out, like always.

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:10.000
You don't want to do this.
-I don't.

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:11.734
I'm looking for
my personal freedom.

00:08:11.734 --> 00:08:12.968
-Yes.
-You know?

00:08:12.968 --> 00:08:14.634
It starts with trying to get
my ring back,

00:08:14.634 --> 00:08:16.701
but that doesn't work so well.

00:08:16.701 --> 00:08:18.200
-No.
-I get a little angry.

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:21.334
But then I'm looking for
my personal freedom.

00:08:21.334 --> 00:08:23.200
There's a whole bunch of
new characters

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:25.901
who are opening up the world
of the High Table.

00:08:25.901 --> 00:08:27.334
-Who plays Caine?

00:08:27.334 --> 00:08:29.267
-Caine is Donnie Yen.

00:08:29.267 --> 00:08:30.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:30.434 --> 00:08:32.300
He's a legend.

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:36.100
Hiroyuki Sanada, Rina Sawayama,
who was on your show.

00:08:36.100 --> 00:08:39.033
-Rina Sawayama is fantastic.
She was on last night.

00:08:39.033 --> 00:08:41.467
-She's awesome.
-It's a crusher cast.

00:08:41.467 --> 00:08:44.667
-Shamier Anderson.
So we have The Tracker.

00:08:44.667 --> 00:08:47.300
We have Caine, we have Shimazu,

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:48.834
so all of these
different characters.

00:08:48.834 --> 00:08:51.701
It's friendship, brotherhood,
father, daughter,

00:08:51.701 --> 00:08:56.701
the choices you make, rules and
consequences, who are you, man?

00:08:56.701 --> 00:08:58.400
-Wow! Come on!

00:08:58.400 --> 00:09:00.400
-Who are we?
-Whoo!

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:02.367
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:09:02.367 --> 00:09:05.334
Here is Keanu Reeves
in "John Wick: Chapter 4."

00:09:05.334 --> 00:09:06.834
Take a look at this.

00:09:06.834 --> 00:09:09.033
♪♪

00:09:09.033 --> 00:09:11.501
-John?

00:09:11.501 --> 00:09:12.767
-Caine.

00:09:21.667 --> 00:09:23.601
They gave you my name.

00:09:26.801 --> 00:09:28.100
-Yeah.

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:32.901
-I'm sorry.

00:09:34.834 --> 00:09:36.300
-Me too.

00:09:46.634 --> 00:09:50.534
-No, no, no! Come on! Cinema!

00:09:50.534 --> 00:09:53.367
Keanu Reeves,
"John Wick: Chapter 4" is

00:09:53.367 --> 00:09:56.634
in theaters and IMAX March 24th.

00:09:56.634 --> 00:09:59.467
Keanu and I are playing
"Pup Quiz" after the break.

00:09:59.467 --> 00:10:00.467
